{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Full.</b> Children and money." "<b>And YHWH has answered [ענה] me.</b> Some say it is from the root of 'to answer [ענות] before me,' but in my opinion it is from the root of 'you shall not answer [תענה] your fellow,' like the sense of 'renew [your] reckoning against me.'" "<b>And Shaddai has brought evil [הרע] upon me.</b> Like 'afflict' [נגע]. And similar to it: 'and creates evil [רע].' Or, 'brought evil upon me' for my transgressions, or it speaks in the language of human beings, and that is the correct [reading]." "<b>The heh of 'return [שבה].'</b> The heh of knowledge, like 'is found here.'" "<b>And the sense of 'and Naomi returned [ותשב].'</b> A second time, to join the time that they came at the beginning of the barley harvest, for the sake of Ruth the gleaner."], :book :ruth, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ruth -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ruth"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:24.054455487Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}